    "problem_statement": "WebsocketConsumer connect method immediately closes connection\n\n#### Description\n\nThe default `connect` method in `WebsocketConsumer` is automatically closing the connection immediately after accepting it, making it impossible to maintain an open websocket connection.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom channels.generic.websocket import WebsocketConsumer\n\nclass MyConsumer(WebsocketConsumer):\n    def receive(self, text_data):\n        self.send(text_data=f\"Echo: {text_data}\")\n\n# When connecting to this consumer, the connection is immediately closed\n# after the handshake, preventing any message exchange\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when using the default `connect` method without overriding it. The connection gets accepted but then immediately terminated, which breaks the expected websocket behavior where the connection should remain open for bidirectional communication."
  }
